<!--
  CLASS NEGATIVE for clause 8.7.1.1: the device class is Input ('scnr'), not
  ColorSpace.

  The 'scnr' half of a pair with HdrDisplayMetadata ('mntr'), so that neither
  class surviving outside the sub-class can be admitted by a classifier that
  tests only one of them.  Everything else 8.7.1.1 requires is satisfied -
  RGB, PCSXYZ, a conforming PQ cicpTag - so each fixture isolates the class
  condition alone.

  The amendment addresses this shape directly: a Display or Input profile
  carrying cicpTag and HAGC "is functionally similar, in terms of tone-mapping
  capability, to an HDR ColorSpace Profile under this clause, but is not one".
  Nothing is reported against it; it is an ordinary Input profile.

  WHAT THIS FIXTURE USED TO BE.  Under clause 8.10 it was a CONFORMING
  Input-class HDR Profile carrying HDR Display metadata, and it pinned two
  things that no longer exist: the 8.10.5 scope note (HDR Display entries in a
  profile that is not 'mntr' drew an Information diagnostic) and the HDR-09
  ruling (the AToBx/BToAx pairing rule was confined to the Display class, so
  an Input profile with AToB0 and no BToA0 was conforming).  The revision
  deletes 8.10.5 outright and states the pairing rule once, unscoped, in
  8.7.1.5 - there is only one class now - so both are gone.  Its DERH, DCV and
  DRWL entries went with the clause.

  It keeps AToB0 without BToA0, which is legal for an Input profile and is now
  simply not this amendment's business.

  EXPECTED CLASSIFICATION is icHdrProfileHdrContent; expected validation
  verdict is `valid`.
--><IccProfile>
